text.paragraph:
Colistimethate for Injection, USP is a sterile parenteral antibiotic product which, when reconstituted (see 
                        Reconstitution
                     ), is suitable for intramuscular or intravenous administration.

Postmarketing cases of renal tubulopathy (i.e., Pseudo-Bartter syndrome) have been identified with the use of intravenous colistimethate sodium (see 
                              ADVERSE REACTIONS
                           ). All cases reported hypokalemia and metabolic alkalosis. Other common findings included hypocalcemia, hypomagnesemia, increased potassium in the urine, normal serum creatinine, and normal blood pressure. Consider electrolyte monitoring during treatment. Normalization of electrolyte abnormalities may require drug discontinuation.
